A||||9||Nashco||88 Offset vs. Others||||5||
Z||000000||Nashco||03-24-2001||06:15 PM||||Hey everyone, I'm having some problems finding the specific info on 88 offset versus others.  I want to buy some wheels that are currently on a earlier year than my 88.  They fit just right on the other car, but I know that my offset is different.  After some research, I want to say the fronts have 7mm more offset (35 older, 42 on mine), and the rears are the same offset.<P>Is this true?  I tried searching the archives, and looking through all of my bookmarked pages, but can't find any exact specs.<P>If this is true, then the rears would be just right, and the fronts would stick out 7mm more than they're supposed to.  7mm wouldn't be too noticeable, and I would just add a spacer in the rear to even them up if need be.  How would this effect handling?  I wouldn't think it'd be noticeable, but some of you have experience with this I'm sure.<P>Thanks for your help, in advance!<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||5
Z||000001||1FST2M6||03-25-2001||11:50 AM||||ther is no offset difference just a wider outer lip ont eh rear wheels yeilding teh 7 to 7.5or 8" rear wheels that came ont eh88 GT and Formulas. (i had the wrong in for i esmailed ya.) <P>Raydar.. 88 Database Guy and RodrV6.. you see this!!! Help me out! ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Raydar||03-25-2001||12:48 PM||||The 15x7 wheels (front and rear, 86 & 87; rear only, 88) are the same casting for all years, although they have different GM part numbers due do different paint colors. The 88 fronts are 15x6, with most of the missing inch coming from the front face of the wheel. I believe the backspacing is very similar for all. <BR>I've seen some 7" wheels on the front of 88s. I think they stick out too far, but that is just an opinion. If the normal front tire size (205-60-15) is used, it may look a bit better. <BR>As for handling? Your steering effort and kickback when you hit potholes will probably be increased just a bit. <BR>This is <B>not</B> the voice of experience, though. I've never tried it.<BR>Maybe some other folks will jump in?<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 T-top Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe||||reg||1
Z||000003||Nashco||03-25-2001||02:29 PM||||That's what I was trying to get figured out Raydar, I think you explained it a lot better than I was asking!  I think if I were to put the same size wheel on the front as the rear, the fronts would stick out farther than the rears.<P>I'm not too worried about steering effort, I'm still a young buck, so that's no biggie.  The looks is what I'm trying to figure out.  Does anyone have pics of an 88 with earlier wheels on it?  That would be a ton of help.  If it doesn't look too bad up front, I would use a spacer in the rear to even them up.  I'm also worried if they stick out more than stock that they might throw more stuff at the car.<P>I guess what I'm trying to clarify is this: the 88 front suspension is wider than earlier years, right?  This would attribute to the loss of the front lip when a smaller rim was used.<P>Thanks for your help, keep shooting ideas/knowledge/opinions this way, and pictures would be a ton of help!<P>I want to snatch these wheels up before somebody else does if they'll work ok.<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000004||NoWing87||03-25-2001||10:34 PM||||Nash...I don't have any numbers for you, but I do have one experience. I put 15x7 Grand Am wheels on my 88...50s up front, 55s on back...no clearance problems. Put the same wheel/tires on my 87, had clearance problems on both ends. That tells me there is more room under the 88s.<BR>Hope it's helpful, Alan||||reg||1
Z||000005||Raydar||03-25-2001||10:53 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Nashco:<BR><B><BR>I guess what I'm trying to clarify is this: the 88 front suspension is wider than earlier years, right?<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yes. It's wider. By about 3/4 inch on each side.<P>The Spotters Guide gives these figures:<BR>Tread, front 84-87.....57.8"<BR>             88 coupe..59.3<BR>             88 GT.....59.7 <P>It also gives different figures for the rear, but I don't see how they could change since all years use the same rear wheels, axles and hubs.<P>Hope I didn't add to the confusion.<P>My7Fieros has a Formula with 7" wheels on the front. He posted pics several months ago. Looked good. Don't know what size tires he's got, tho'. I've also seen a pic of a GT with 15x7s and 215's on the front. Thought it looked strange.  <P><BR>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 T-top Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe<p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 03-25-2001).]||||reg||1
